Map<String,String> allowed = Map.of("name","name", "date","created_at");
String col = allowed.get(sortCol);
if (col == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("bad sort column");

String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE active = ? ORDER BY " + col;  // col from allow-list
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql)) {
    ps.setBoolean(1, true);   // values still bound
    ps.executeQuery();
}
```

```java
// even though 'name' came from our own DB, treat it as untrusted
String name = rs.getString("username");
String sql = "SELECT * FROM logs WHERE user = ?";
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql)) {
    ps.setString(1, name);   // bound as data on EVERY query, not just input
    ps.executeQuery();
}
```

*Parameterize whenever you build a query — at input and at every later use of stored data.*
